2026-08-09T14:38:23.9147392Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9147872Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9148345Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9149142Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9149556Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9149956Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9150451Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9150942Z [36;1m# the *package's* runtime parallelism, not compilation, so this is safe.[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9151770Z [36;1mncores="$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'n <- parallel::detectCores(); cat(if (is.na(n) || n < 1) 2L else as.integer(n))')"[0m
2026-08-09T14:38:23.9152339Z [36;1mecho "MAKEFLAGS = -j${ncores}" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
